WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.410
And now, the third place match

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:06.110
between Kawachi and Suwabara is all that
remains in the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.130
For the sake of this match,
upon Matsushiro’s recommendation,

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.610
St. Andrew’s Church

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.990
For the sake of this match,
upon Matsushiro’s recommendation,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.450
Kawachi knocked on the door of St. Andrew’s Church, but...

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.830
That’s because you’re a
“What was that?!” person.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.330
What was that?!

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.970
You are bound by common sense

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.340
and are always surprised by the geniuses in the end.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.830
You’re just a side character shouting “What was that?!”

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.800
That is your true nature.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.740
What was that?!

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.390
What was that?! What was that?!

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.910
Well, you must.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.460
Throw away common sense.
Get yourself an afro.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.710
Thus, he overcame the “What
was that?!” person within himself.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.840
However...

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.440
I’m sorry to tell you that
the nun you met is...

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.190
A FAKE!

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.030
What was that?!

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.800
You...

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.730
big fool!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.300
You absolutely can’t win!

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.190
Originally developed as a lethal
weapon to use in the finals...

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.300
My ultimate French bread.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.790
You can’t win against my Dancing French Bread!!

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.100
What was that?!

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.310
Ouch!

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.830
That’s right.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.310
I shouldn’t be saying “What was that?!”

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.330
Right now, I have an afro.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.820
I won’t lose so easily.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.320
Believe in yourself, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.130
Listen up, Suwabara.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.080
While your French bread may
dance, my French bread can sing!

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.360
Huh?

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.460
I’m looking forward to that, Kawachi.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.460
But, Suwabara has already begun baking his bread.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.960
What was that?!

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:57.950
It’s no use, is it?

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.240
It’s no use.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.980
Yeah, it’s no use.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.970
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.080
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.330
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.940
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:18.010
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.890
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:39.100
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:47.060
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:54.940
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:02.660
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:10.090
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:19.510
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:28.230
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.480
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.480
is the light of only you.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:39.230
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:44.080
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:51.760
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.910
The last match of the Newcomers’ Battle!!

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.330
The Singing and Dancing French Breads!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.220
What was that?!

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.480
And suddenly, out of nowhere,
I feel cold stares piercing me.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.910
They’re mad...

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.910
This isn’t good...

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.480
I did it again.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.700
This isn’t the time to be worried about others.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.490
I must focus on myself.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.580
All right, this is the finishing touch!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.080
I’ll start baking, too.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.750
What is Kawachi-san...?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.760
He skewered it to make holes,
eliminating the need to slash it...

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.800
but to put all that water into the bucket...

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.270
It’s to regulate the steam.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:52.600
What?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.440
The reason that the surface of
French bread is hard is that...

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.360
the tiny droplets of water

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.700
that are sticking to the surface of the
dough are dried at a high temperature.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.610
You know that, right, Tsukino?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.320
Yes, of course.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:11.290
For that reason, the oven that’s being
used will have the facility to produce steam.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:16.510
During the baking process,
the oven will be filled with steam,

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.540
such that drops of water
stick to the surface of the dough.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.470
However...

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:24.850
that only helps in making a regular French bread.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.560
It can’t release more than a fixed amount of steam.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.940
Most likely, after testing many things,

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:35.100
Kawachi has determined that
this is what suits his bread the best.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.150
I see.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.310
But still, it’s a lot of water.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.380
With this, we’re done.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.290
How’s it looking, Suwabara?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.370
Your bread, that is...

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.210
Don’t talk to me.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.120
How about you concentrate on your own baking?

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.330
There’s no need.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.220
When my bread’s done,

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.810
it’ll let me know...

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.470
by singing!

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.590
What?!

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.320
The water in the bucket has started
boiling and letting off steam, hasn’t it?

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.240
It’s a nice melody.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:28.110
To me, it sounds like the shrill of
cicadas announcing the advent of summer.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:28.820
And then...!

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:34.880
What the...?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.880
Some strange sound is...

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.830
It kind of sounds like a flute...

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.800
No, that is not it.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.040
The bread is crying.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.180
No way!

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.510
That’s amazing!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.670
A crying bread, eh?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.270
Uhh... no, wait a moment...

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.480
This isn’t crying,

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.640
it’s singing!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.480
Don’t you think it’s kinda going la-la-la...?

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:03.110
Your hairstyle was enough to frighten me,

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.700
but the fact that your bread is crying also frightens me.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.410
I’m looking forward to tasting it.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:08.860
No... well, you see...

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.750
Like I said... It’s singing...

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:11.870
A crying bread!
Like I said... It’s singing...

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.080
You embarrassing little...

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.580
No, it’s not like that...

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.750
But, Kawachi,

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.580
don’t think that that’s enough
to let you win!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.980
Not against this Dancing French Bread!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.140
I-It looks like a snake!

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.220
The bread’s moving like a snake!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.220
Oh, I see!

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.480
Suwabara’s bread was unusually long!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.690
He must have hung that long
bread from the top with something,

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.940
then coiled it like a snake
before putting it into the oven!

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:44.740
And then...

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:46.950
The moment the bread was exposed to the outside,

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.030
due to the change in temperature,
the steam pressure within the bread changed,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.880
leading to the appearance of movement.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.290
But, while it may look like it’s moving...

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.330
it doesn’t appear to be dancing.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.040
And as a bread that’s simply long...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.250
With such a bread...

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.080
you rea~lly can’t win against me.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.380
Kawachi.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.340
Your bread still isn’t done, is it?

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.300
Not yet.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.850
Until this bread’s wailing – I mean
singing, stops, it’s not finished baking.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.310
Is that so?

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.310
In that case, I request that my bread be sampled first.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.970
Who’ll be doing the judging?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.320
Meister, is it you?

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:21.680
Me, me!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.240
With the Meister having exhausted the supplies for his tricks, he’s in “I am tired” mode.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.730
So, I’m in charge.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.730
But, I could have done it...!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.370
And if I was to say no?

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.360
What?!

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.660
In the semifinals against Azuma,

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.830
you didn’t even taste my bread!

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.540
Shut up, shut up.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.210
Just eat my croissant without saying anything.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.370
If you do so...

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.470
Will I be able to go to heaven?

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.430
What?!

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.470
Dave-sensei and I went to
heaven because of Azuma’s bread.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.640
As long as I can’t go to heaven with your bread...

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.970
it’s your loss.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.690
I don’t want such a person
eating my Dancing French Bread.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.530
What are you, a child?

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.490
Still holding a grudge over a little thing like that?!

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:11.830
Just let me eat it!

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:12.780
Shut up!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.870
You’re like a spoiled child yourself!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.030
Moreover, you’re too full of yourself!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:21.660
What a cheap little...

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:27.220
Eating it with that annoying expression!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.470
Both of you are such children...

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.880
By the way...
What was it you were thinking earlier?

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.630
Earlier...?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.730
After seeing my bread, you thought that
it was just moving, rather than dancing?!

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:41.350
And I bet you also thought that it was “just long,” right?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.190
I-I don’t know what you’re talking about...

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.230
How can he be so sharp?

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.350
That’s why you’re only second-class!

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.360
What was that?!

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.280
Dammit...

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.370
I said it again.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.360
Look at that.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.740
What?

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.250
Kuro-yan’s dancing!

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.880
It isn’t the bread that dances?!

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.970
Who said that it’d be the bread that dances?

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:12.920
This is...

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.420
a French bread so delicious that
anyone who eats it starts to dance!

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.390
That’s so foolish!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.350
Foolish, you say?

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.980
If it’s a fool who dances, and a fool who watches...

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.230
If both are fools...

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:27.060
you might as well dance!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.230
Might as well. Might as well. Might as well.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.570
I don’t know what to think about awa
odori being performed in that costume...

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:36.240
Or, rather...
The SP’s haven’t eaten the bread.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.910
Did you see that, Kawachi?

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.550
This is what’s remarkable about the Dancing Bread!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.330
W-What kind of man is he?!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:47.750
You mean, he even calculated the
reaction before making the bread?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.630
But...

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.510
why is a French bread that’s just long so delicious?

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.750
Let me explain that.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:57.600
The dance has changed again.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.100
The l-lambada...? In that costume...?

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.730
And a pretty weird one, at that.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:03.900
Listen up.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.480
Fundamentally, French bread
is more delicious the longer it is.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.570
As you know...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:12.400
the basis of French bread is a bread
with a hard surface and a soft interior.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.030
To make the inside soft,

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:18.740
all you have to do is make the
crumb, or the white interior, long.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:23.420
The bigger the crumb is, the
more air gets trapped inside,

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.740
giving you a light consistency.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:27.750
Is that so?

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.880
They say that...

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.880
in 17th century France,

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.750
gluttony was an indication of status amongst the rich.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.100
Amongst those rich people,

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.430
the French king, Louis XIV,

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.730
who had about 344 chefs employed under him,

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.760
especially liked big things.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.230
Claiming that they were delicious,

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:51.030
he had extremely long breads made.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.150
See, see?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.450
It’s long, long!

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:54.270
Louis, Louis.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.410
When the French Revolution began,

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:00.330
the chefs were no longer able to work at the palace.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.620
So, they went into the city and opened up restaurants.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:07.280
In the pursuit of great taste, they began
competing over the length of their breads.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.630
The Montmartre champion is...

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.550
Argo Rushie!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.260
However, long bread was difficult to even store.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.190
It was a symbol of extravagance.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:23.110
Napoleon hated that, and therefore decided
what the length of French bread should be.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.280
This is not right.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.360
He went through the trouble of wearing
that costume in order to explain that...

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.230
I hadn’t included any of that in my calculations, either...

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:33.860
Either way,

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.700
I knew that he had decided on the length on his own,

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.730
but to think that there was such a reason behind it...

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.450
To not even know that...

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.120
That’s why I said...

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.490
that you’re second-class!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.950
W-What did you say?!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.460
Hey, Manager...

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.340
is “What did you say?!” all right?

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.250
Hmm... it might be just barely okay.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:54.710
You’re second-class...!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.670
What did you say?!

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:59.640
Just because I wasn’t saying anything, you can’t just say whatever you like!

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:03.390
It may be that longer bread is delicious. I don’t care.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:05.340
That’s all there is to your trick, right?

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:12.020
Any moment now, my bread’s
wail – I mean song, will stop.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.310
Once that happens, I’ll show you...

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:18.060
my Singing French Bread!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:30.960
Any moment now, my bread’s
wail – I mean song, will stop.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.240
Once that happens, I’ll show you...

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.750
my Singing French Bread!

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.470
Hey, Manager,

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:42.640
I think that Kawachi has finally gotten ahold of himself.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:43.710
So it seems.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.270
More importantly, Azuma...

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:46.560
What are you going to do?

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.020
Huh? About what?

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.360
Are you going? To the Main Branch...

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.060
That’s right...

00:13:55.650 --> 00:14:00.910
Winning means that Azuma-san will be awarded the privilege of going to the Main Branch.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.700
Once he goes to the Main Branch,
his pay will be triple that of ours.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.070
Our facilities can’t compare
to theirs, either.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.320
It’s obvious that anyone would go to the Main Branch.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.870
I’m not going.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.130
Or is there some kind of rule saying that I must go?

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.920
It’ll be troublesome if that’s the case...

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.840
There’s no such rule, but...

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:20.800
Why?

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:25.510
I may not have told you this, but...

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.980
the pay at the Main Branch is three times that of ours.

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:30.600
Also...

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:34.230
Their facilities are amazing enough
to give no cause for complaints either.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.930
You want me to leave, Tsukino?

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.100
N-Not at all...!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.280
If my salary were to increase threefold,

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:46.160
would I be able to reach the true
<i>Japan</i> three times as fast, Tsukino?

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.330
I wouldn’t know something like that.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.790
Going to the Main Branch isn’t my dream.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.240
Mine is to make the <i>Japan</i>.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.710
And I have...

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.210
Kawachi,

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.710
Tsukino,

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.710
Manager...

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.210
And, umm... there’s that
what’s-his-name guy, too.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.720
I like that store.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.090
Azuma-san.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.690
Is that so?

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:15.310
But, what if Kawachi was to leave?

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.060
Stop!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:24.070
Even a moronic brain like yours should get a good idea if you increase your wrinkles a little.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.330
You and Kawachi have been friends through
good times and bad since joining the store.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.320
You’re rivals who help each other grow.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.870
And as a team,

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:38.370
you’ve become an important
existence to us.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.590
But, unlike you, Kawachi

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:43.590
wants to go to the Main Branch
to make life easier for his family.

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:47.840
Should he place third, he would apply
to go to the Main Branch without a doubt.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.020
Even then, I’ll stay.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.390
Kawachi is Kawachi,

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:53.840
and I’m me.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.550
Very well.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:59.900
Then, both of us should be prepared.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.560
You as well, Tsukino.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.950
Look!

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.900
This is my Singing French Bread.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.910
Double Crust!

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.420
Double Crust?

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.040
If you’re going to eat it, it’s best when
it’s freshly baked, Kuro-yan.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.370
Stop with the Kuro-yan.

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:24.370
The crust refers to the surface of the bread.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.680
If he’s calling it a double crust,

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:30.060
does it mean that the surface is two times as thick?

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:31.100
No...

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:35.390
While it looks like a thick crust, it doesn’t
appear to be double the usual thickness...

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.730
No matter.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:39.360
Once I eat it, all my questions should be answered.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.620
That’s right...

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.990
This is from the time...

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:50.360
when I was still in high school in America...

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.360
You’re amazing, Ryou.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.750
You did it again, didn’t you?

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.120
You’re the best in the school again.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.870
His name was Kid.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.210
Yeah, Kid.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:03.370
Kid was an older classmate,
and my best friend.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:07.090
After becoming the best in the
school, he’s acting like it’s nothing.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.140
He’ll probably skip grades again.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.250
He’s really annoying.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.430
Ryou.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.390
Don’t worry about guys like that.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:18.470
They’re just jealous that they can’t compare to you.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:21.060
In addition to being Japanese,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.690
I was always the object of envy,
due to my having skipped grades.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.690
Yet, he would encourage me.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.200
In fights, and while hitting on women.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.990
He would listen to my complaints.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.450
We were together in whatever we did.

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.370
And...

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:38.200
He did anything for me, without ever
making it seem like he didn’t want to.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:43.040
When I was weakened in mind
and body after too much studying,

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.510
he performed a medical examination on me.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:46.540
No, I didn’t.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.790
When I was homesick,

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.220
he would take the place of my mother.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.300
No, I didn’t.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.600
When I was broke...

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.770
he would raise money from somewhere and give it to me, without restraint.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:02.310
Don’t make things up.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.570
But, one day...

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:05.810
Hey, Ryou...

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.900
Actually... I failed again.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.870
Is that so?

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.900
Hey, Kid...

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.280
Right now, you’re truly...

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.500
a Double Classmate.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.330
That’s true, but...

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.170
Shortened to...

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:21.290
You’re going to shorten it?

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:25.710
Double Crust!

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.260
I don’t understand the meaning of that.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.970
Kid...

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:32.250
what are you doing these days...?

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:34.850
Hey, Manager...

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:37.260
why is Old Man Kuroyanagi crying?

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:44.750
This match is a draw...

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.780
Both of you stand at third place!

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.570
Don’t mess with me!

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:52.610
I can’t accept a draw!

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.610
What the hell is a Double Crust?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.660
Explain it properly, Kuroyanagi.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:01.920
Double Crust is from when I was in high school...

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.290
Kuro-yan doesn’t need to explain it.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.330
This second-class person here
can explain it.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.050
I think you know this, but...

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:11.840
the crust refers to the surface of the bread.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:16.960
And my Double Crust involves
having one more crust than the usual.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.060
Right, Kuro-yan?

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:22.350
At that time, I was the object of people’s envy for constantly skipping grades...

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.230
Kid always...

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.400
Listen up!

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:26.390
My bread...

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:30.860
involves making air sacs by
spearing the bread with chopsticks,

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.400
such that, at the ends, they make a large pocket of air.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.200
Before baking it, I removed all of the chopsticks,

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:41.290
leaving a dough that’s rather like an ocarina or recorder.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:44.410
I placed that on top of the bucket and baked it.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.170
Therefore, the steam that comes out of the bucket

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:51.410
would pass through the vents
in the bread and play a tune.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:55.610
Also, the sound is produced through
the vents created by the chopsticks

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:58.370
until the expansion due to fermentation is complete.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:01.420
However, the real aim isn’t to produce the sound.

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:04.480
By allowing steam to pass through the dough,

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:06.940
it creates a crust within the dough as well.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.400
That was my objective!

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:09.650
Impossible!

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.400
A crust within the dough?!

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.450
Ah, Kid...

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:16.230
My youth... Because you were there for me...

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:18.830
I see.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.700
The crust is formed when the dough,

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.250
with water droplets sticking to it,
is baked at a high temperature.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.080
Kawachi decided to make
crust within the dough as well.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:30.120
By making holes in the dough,
water droplets could stick in there.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.960
In other words, Double Classmate.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.550
Shortened to...

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:36.960
Double Crust!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.680
What do you think, Suwabara?

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.100
Are you quaking in fear yet?

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.470
It’s me who should be upset
about the draw.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.300
Kawachi.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:46.730
Hold this and see.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.400
Suwabara’s bread?

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:51.140
I-It’s light.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.190
It’s really light...

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.440
Even though it’s so big.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.900
It might be lighter than my French bread.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.780
The flour I used to make this bread

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.040
is pretty much the same as
the flour used in your bread.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:05.960
While kneading it, I trapped a large amount of air inside,

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:08.280
and then extended it to that length.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.210
It’s true that the basis of French bread

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:13.800
is to have a hard crust and soft insides.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:14.420
But...

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:18.090
to think that you made it so long
with the same flour that I used...

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:21.500
Do the two of you understand now?

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.180
Kawachi’s idea

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:27.510
was to make a wonderful French
bread not shackled by common sense.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.190
In comparison, Suwabara’s bread

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:32.190
involved using the basics of making French bread

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.730
to trap a large amount of air within the dough,

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:37.520
taking the bread to the limits of how soft it can be.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.520
It’s just as wonderful a bread.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.410
Therefore, it’s a draw.

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:42.900
Both of you are third place winners.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:46.540
You really are one hell of a baker.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.880
Hats off to you.

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:52.040
I feel nothing at being
complimented by a second-class baker.

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:53.550
What did you say?!

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:54.790
However...

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:57.590
If I think of them as the words of a first class baker,

00:21:57.590 --> 00:22:00.130
I seem to be able to accept it
quite naturally.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:02.300
It doesn’t feel wrong.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:04.800
Suwabara...

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:08.030
And now, we shall move on to the awards ceremony.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:14.820
Manager!

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.190
Kawachi is third place.

00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:16.850
He did it!

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:18.730
Yeah.

00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:21.910
With this, Kawachi-san can reach his objective

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:24.540
of employment at the Main Store.

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:30.460
It’s finally time for him to make a decision.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.450 --> 00:24:06.400
What’s this?

00:24:06.400 --> 00:24:08.160
Cooking in three minutes?

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:08.800
Next week,

00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:12.290
we will introduce a <i>Japan</i> that even an amateur should be able to make easily.

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:13.200
Make sure to keep some paper...

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:14.370
Handy, ok?

00:24:14.370 --> 00:24:15.870
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:17.500
Let’s all make bread together!!

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:18.960
It’s <i>Japan</i> #2!

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:25.340
The man who loved the long French bread,

00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:26.340
Louis XIV.

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:28.770
He was the French monarch who
constructed the famous Palace of Versailles.

00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:31.140
He was also known as the Sun King.

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:31.710
Louis, Louis.

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:34.480
Really?!
